{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/124434-should-lunars-be-able-to-magically-affect-the-world-around-them","id":124434,"title":"Should Lunars be able to magically affect the world around them?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-05-03T06:12:31-07:00","id":124434,"title":"Should Lunars be able to magically affect the world around them?","content":"With all the recent talk about Sorcery and Astrology, I got to thinking about how each splat expresses its power. Most do so in an external capacity, that is, they affect the world outside of themselves. Even Solars, whose native powers enhance their natural abilities, still get things like Wyld-Shaping and Solar Circle Sorcery! And Sidereals prayer strip charms are all over that, before you even get to SMA (and, in theory, astrology). <br /> <br /> Lunars seem a bit left behind here. Knacks can be useful and powerful, but by definition, only affect the Lunar themselves (or sometimes, one other person). SHOULD Lunars have a subsystem that affects the world around them?<br /> <br /> I came up with such a thing awhile ago: The idea was basically that the Primordials had built all sorts of &quot;back door&quot; shortcut codes into Creation, distinct from what would be called Shaping/Sorcery. Luna (in a nod to Isis stealing the secrets of magic from Ra) spent millenia stealing these secrets from various Titans, through trickery, seduction, contests, what have you. She squirreled this secret knowledge away for when it might prove useful, never really needing it herself; when the Primordial War approached, she gave these secrets to her Chosen, who have passed them down mainly through their Priestly Caste, ever since (perhaps another reason the No Moons wiped them out, to assimilate this arcane wisdom).<br /> <br /> These Rites (can you think of a better word for them?<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />\u200b) would be a way for Lunars to mystically affect the world around them, in ways large and small. Some charms that already do this, like the Ritual of Lunar Stability, Moonsilver tattoo fixing or even Eagle-Fish Prophecy, could be made into Rites instead. The more powerful ones could even rival SCS or SMA, which would give mystical or trickster-oriented Lunars other avenues of effectiveness rather than &quot;become big terrifying creature&quot;, which is the main thing their current subsystem of Knacks allows for. <br /> <br /> Of course, Rites would have to be mechanically distinct from Sorcery. Beastman creation and Genesis effects coming from Rites could answer the problems some people have such things as written. If Rites aren't Shaping effects, they provide an easy way to get through Shaping Defenses, which would probably be TOO powerful...<br /> <br /> Thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-03T07:18:25-07:00","id":124469,"title":"","content":"Why do you feel that they NEED a distinct subsystem to do this? Their Charms allow them to gain ownership of tracts of land, use the Wyld to their advantage, and other deeds to affect the world around them. Not to mention that they have access to Sorcery/Necromancy.<br /> <br /> I, personally, do not see a need for another subsystem just for lunars. What we do need, is more Charms for them. Solars got a lot of spotlight in terms of Charms beyond their basic set, as did Abyssals, Infernals, and even Dragon-Blooded. Lunars received much less of a content here, and could really use it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/721-greyskull","name":"Greyskull","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-03T07:46:54-07:00","id":124483,"title":"","content":"Personally, I like the idea that Lunars shape the world around them manually - by becoming a Yeddim or a Tyrant Lizard and physically building/destroying/helping in construction.<br /> <br /> The issue I see is that Thaumaturgy (Geomancy) is pretty flat and useless for Exalts - I'd love for a Lunar to hulk out, spend a montage landscaping and end up with a really cool Geomantic effect (that could go for other splats as well, but the unique Lunar powerset more easily allows them to do this alone and bare-handed). And I think that powers specific to Lunars should enhance the Lunar's ability to build and change the environment rather than change the environment for them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-03T12:20:22-07:00","id":124668,"title":"","content":"So, some kind of suped-up Thaumaturgy and Geomancy?<br /> <br /> Well... geomancy involves a lot of placement, don't it? So... hrm...<br /> <br /> Maybe there are less-than-obvious placements that can get some effects that everyone else thought were impossible. Like, a mortal geomancer will tell you, &quot;No, I can't do shit to get water out here.&quot; A Lunar, with all the secrets the Moon ferreted away from the Titans, extrapolated herself and later her chosen built upon, will say, &quot;Yeah, I can make water happen.&quot;<br /> <br /> This would encourage Lunars to spend their time in the middle of fucking nowhere, because these project need a ton of room. It's also how they go society building, doing stuff no mortal geomancer can figure out how to do but will sustain itself as long as nobody kicks it over.<br /> <br /> Sidereals can't do it. You can fluff it that these're secrets that the Maidens couldn't steal, it wasn't their nature, and so neither can their Chosen. Maybe, it's a minor Blasphemy effect. Solars can grasp it, if they have a Lunar teacher, but they have the same limitations if they learned SMA.<br /> <br /> And I'm always in favor of Terrestrials getting to do stuff if you get enough of them in the same spot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1252-god_of_awesome","name":"God_of_Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1252_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-03T12:46:29-07:00","id":124691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Greyskull</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/124434-should-lunars-be-able-to-magically-affect-the-world-around-them?p=124469#post124469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why do you feel that they NEED a distinct subsystem to do this?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would agree with Greyskull on this. <br /> <br /> It's not like Terrestrials can <i>only</i> manipulate the elements, or Sidereals can <i>only</i> do Astrology or Solars can <i>only</i> behave as though the sun shines out of their butt. These are all things they're good at doing, not things that they're limited to doing and need special permission to work around. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1849-suddenthunder","name":"SuddenThunder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1849_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-03T14:30:48-07:00","id":124769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kukla</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm with SuddenThunder and Greyskull. This doesn't need to be a distinct subsystem.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless you wanted to go the route of teaching it to Solars.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, yeah, it could just be a distinct theme of Lunar charms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1252-god_of_awesome","name":"God_of_Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1252_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-03T14:42:32-07:00","id":124778,"title":"","content":"If they were to do this, it would be secrets gleaned from Gaia pillowtalk from Luna, shared through visions and practise to her chosen, because Luna finds it interesting or some other mythological reason. I just like the idea it's a power they adopted, rather than a power natural to them. It also explains how only Lunars can do it, because it's their patron which is favoured (nailing) Gaia, not the UCS, and not the Maidens, and certainly not the Elemental Dragons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-03T14:48:17-07:00","id":124780,"title":"","content":"Has there been some spoiler that I missed that &quot;territory control&quot; is going to be a theme for Lunars in 3E like it kinda was in 2E? 'cause if not, I feel that any Lunar who wants to control an area like this would be using more conventional means like Sorcery and Geomancy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-03T14:51:44-07:00","id":124783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JayTee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/124434-should-lunars-be-able-to-magically-affect-the-world-around-them?p=124780#post124780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Has there been some spoiler that I missed that &quot;territory control&quot; is going to be a theme for Lunars in 3E like it kinda was in 2E? 'cause if not, I feel that any Lunar who wants to control an area like this would be using more conventional means like Sorcery and Geomancy.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think there was, but its fun to speculate.<br /> <br /> I'd like to think there's a fundamental difference between Geomancy and Lunar Geomancy, like the difference between Martial Arts, and Sidereal Martial Arts. It's unique to them, learned in some way, and possible to teach to Solars but with great disfavour since it's based on the connection between Luna and Gaia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-03T14:59:15-07:00","id":124791,"title":"","content":"Mind you, Lunars in 2E can influence the world around them via Grace magic, as all Lunars (and Eclipse) can use them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1661-zeroregistry","name":"ZeroRegistry","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-03T16:16:50-07:00","id":124839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>God_of_Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/124434-should-lunars-be-able-to-magically-affect-the-world-around-them?p=124668#post124668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, some kind of suped-up Thaumaturgy and Geomancy?<br /> <br /> Well... geomancy involves a lot of placement, don't it? So... hrm...<br /> <br /> Maybe there are less-than-obvious placements that can get some effects that everyone else thought were impossible. Like, a mortal geomancer will tell you, &quot;No, I can't do shit to get water out here.&quot; A Lunar, with all the secrets the Moon ferreted away from the Titans, extrapolated herself and later her chosen built upon, will say, &quot;Yeah, I can make water happen.&quot;<br /> <br /> This would encourage Lunars to spend their time in the middle of fucking nowhere, because these project need a ton of room. It's also how they go society building, doing stuff no mortal geomancer can figure out how to do but will sustain itself as long as nobody kicks it over.<br /> <br /> Sidereals can't do it. You can fluff it that these're secrets that the Maidens couldn't steal, it wasn't their nature, and so neither can their Chosen. Maybe, it's a minor Blasphemy effect. Solars can grasp it, if they have a Lunar teacher, but they have the same limitations if they learned SMA.<br /> <br /> And I'm always in favor of Terrestrials getting to do stuff if you get enough of them in the same spot.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am 100% all for this.<br /> And actually, if we're going by the paradigm that Charms are just magical tricks you picked up, there's plenty of room in Intelligence, and maybe Perception/Manipulation for Geomancy-enhancing charms - &quot;tricking&quot; everyone and Creation into thinking that one type of structure is an other, substituting resources to get effects that aren't normally possible et. al. is a theme I'd love to have in Lunars, or maybe even Terrestrial Cricle Sorcery to a smaller extent (because I also agree with enough terrestrials getting shit done.)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-03T17:50:09-07:00","id":124882,"title":"","content":"I've always been a big fan of Lunar territory and mastery over nature. I like the idea of Lunars calling down blizzards to stymie invaders in their lands, or commanding swarms of biting insects or herds of beasts. I like the idea of Lunars who can dam up rivers to leave the lands downstream barren, or Lunars who can summon up the veil of night to hide their allies. I want Lunars to ride into civilization at the head of great thunderclouds, to command the spirits of the wilderness to do their bidding.<br /> <br /> Now, a lot of that can be sorcery. I'm fine with many of those capabilities being open to non-Lunar exalts: storm-witch Air aspects or Zenith shamans or what-have you. I'm not sure Lunars need something making this thematic territory exclusive to them or making them inherently better at it mechanically, but I'd like to see some stuff in fluff saying they do this sort of thing a lot. Nature-sorcery is a thing Lunars should do lots of, and some indication that it's one of the things elder lunars teach that makes them valuable mentors would be nice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-03T18:18:05-07:00","id":124894,"title":"","content":"@Fata-ku: More like, if you made Exalted Geomancy, and let Lunars get the top levels of it.<br /> <br /> Hrm, actually, forget my Dragon Blooded fetish, let's talk about Exalted Geomancy! Eh, how does this sound?<br /> <br /> God/Terrestrial Degree Geomancy (Alt: Elemental Degree) (Alt: Dragon)<br /> Primordial/Celestial Degree Geomancy (Alt: Incarnae Degree) (Alt: God)<br /> Gaia/Lunar Degree Geomancy (Alt: Primordial Degree)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1252-god_of_awesome","name":"God_of_Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1252_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-03T18:38:39-07:00","id":124903,"title":"","content":"I don't know, I really like the idea of Geomancy consistently working off the same principles for everyone, and Lunars having an advantage because moving more mass = doing more geomancy - and with a score of 29 (Strength 18 (Heavy Weights + 3) + Athletics 5 ( Do you even lift +3) ) you can move a LOT of mass, hence do a LOT more geomancy.<br /> <br /> Although if I did make it to work differently for different splats, it would be something like:<br /> <br /> Solars can make Geomancy so essence-cuttingly precise that [stuff happens]<br /> Lunars stole Primordial secrets* that would physically twist the forms of those not protected by tattoos if pondered too deeply (and using them requires deep pondering) and can [stuff]<br /> Dragonblooded are like ants, and can make geomancy work on a much, much broader scale because of sheer numbers and teamwork, and so [stuff].<br /> Sidereals : err.... reasons? Stuff is as it needs to be or something, and so [stuff] because of [reasons].<br /> Abyssals : Being living beings infused with death gives them power over the memetically maleable Underworld, and so [stuff]<br /> Infernals : AAAAHAHAHAHAHAHAHA!!!! VITRIOL EVERYWHERE! FEEL THE LIQUID HATE FLOW THROUGH YOU!! and so [stuff].<br /> <br /> (I like the primordial-secret-stealing idea tbh)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":43,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","user":"Fata-Ku","date":". 05-03-2014, 09:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-03T19:49:38-07:00","id":124922,"title":"","content":"I, on the other hand, wouldn't mind seeing it as something along the lines of Martial Arts and Sorcery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1252-god_of_awesome","name":"God_of_Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1252_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-03T20:22:14-07:00","id":124941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>God_of_Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/124434-should-lunars-be-able-to-magically-affect-the-world-around-them?p=124922#post124922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I, on the other hand, wouldn't mind seeing it as something along the lines of Martial Arts and Sorcery.</div> </div> </div> </div>Elaborate, please!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-04T07:04:02-07:00","id":125148,"title":"","content":"If you want Lunars to have some supped up facility with some Arts of Thaumaturgy, then go ahead and make custom Charms for them.<br /> <br /> For solars I've added two Occult Charms in my games. One lets them succeed on Thaumaturgy with a threshold of 1 suxxes, and the other lets them perform it faster.<br /> <br /> I can see Lunars getting Charms that give them greater facility with Husbandry, and maybe Weather Working and Geomancy in their territories.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/721-greyskull","name":"Greyskull","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-04T07:42:30-07:00","id":125163,"title":"","content":"It's not something supported in the games, but it's always been my personal head cannon that there's a way of viewing reality that's sort of the default for each kind of Celestial Exalt. <br /> <br /> Solar's tend to see everything in terms of their personal narrative. It's why their interaction with the Wyld isn't so much interaction as <i>&quot;I enforce my will, creating reality</i>&quot; It's also why they can expand dramatically in any direction they choose. Whatever power they're expressing or talent they're showing, it's about their own excellence. It's great for them personally (or not, it could be tragic), but it tends to wrap up others in their personal dreams and coerce them into the Solars personal stories. It helps that Solar's charms and Virtue heavy character flaws support this.<br /> <br /> Sidereal's tend to take the long view, seeing everything holistically (a plus) but in terms of a preordained plan. This is partially why they favor martial arts, the exact kata's, spiritual discipline, and <i>Forms</i> express the Sidereal's need to fit everything into the narrative of Creation and Destiny. It's also why a Sidereal that prepares him or herself is so much more potent, they manipulate their <i>story </i>and the <i>story </i>of others to fit within their plan. This is further supported by the Sidereal's utter refusal to have anything to do with the Wyld, except to destroy it in order to make more Loom directed Creation space.<br /> <br /> The Lunar's are individualists, focusing on the (old world definition) of the term Liberal. This is distinctly different from Solar's <i>personal</i> focus, because the Lunar doesn't need to co-opt others into their story to express it. This is supported by the Lunar's focus on change, adaptability, and <i>Weird magic</i>. In the conversion of Exalted that I'm working on I'm giving Lunar Exalted a form of magic that expands from some base assumptions concerning their geomancy and terrain manipulation charms, called Phantasm.<br /> <br /> Essentially, Phantasm allows Lunar's to break down parts of reality to change it, and themselves while inside this area. Rather than having a charm that directly makes them as big as a small mountain the Lunar would activate Phantasm and shape the terrain based upon a set scale of points, much in the same way that Deathlords can shape the Labyrinth with the right magic. Phantasm here is a bit of a misnomer, it's not that what the Lunar creates or changes isn't real, it's just that the barriers of difference between what the Lunar imagines to be true and what is actually true break down dramatically.<br /> <br /> In terms of the Wyld, the Lunar's don't change it into Creation permanently like Solars, but they do express their individual wishes upon the Wyld on a temporary basis that grants them an incredibly potent degree of control and allows them to rewrite very basic rules of reality that a Solar couldn't achieve on a long term basis without exacting geomancy. While much less<i> bound</i> within the rules of reality than Solar Wyld Shaping, it is also much more temporary<br /> <br /> It kind of goes in an opposite direction from the designers intent to make Lunar's more <i>physical</i> but I like my Lunar's to be more Baba Yaga and less Behemoth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron-crowns.obsidianportal.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron...dianportal.com</a> Visit Golden Shackles, Iron Crowns; a 3rd Edition Exalted Campaign ongoing since 2014","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2711-janissary87","name":"Janissary87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2711_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-04T17:20:23-07:00","id":125403,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't think Lunars should have such effects beyond their Sorcery*, I'd see Lunars as more liable to find a place that has already had some magical juju sunk into it under the many circumstances that might prop up in the Age of Sorrows, effectively kick whatever might already be living there out, and then set themselves up as the hero or monster living comfortably inside of it. I don't think they should be especially built for affecting the world, more for being able to effectively root themselves throughout a world that is distressingly fluid.<br /> <br /> Contemporary Creation is a world of many extreme environments and Lunars are the ultimate extremophiles because, without needing to refine their power to the purpose of overcoming the challenges of extreme environments, any one of them can just snatch up one of the creatures that survives there as a matter of course and become it. A Lunar might flood a valley by strategically breaking dams rather than summoning torrential rains, and then get by there casually by eating one of the accompanying fish. Any Lunar could live comfortably in the area around Chernobyl by hunting the local ducks. They're better off doing this, in a context of a widely collective agenda against enemies who'll do less well, and where the world is breaking down anyway and they widely lack the means to fix it.<br /> <br /> * Noting that it might be that Lunars are still part of a very elite club that can utilise the second circle, although I'd also imagine that their current strategic milieu might mean that they can't quite get the full range out of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-04T19:07:54-07:00","id":125465,"title":"","content":"<br /> Sooo, just realized I didn't really make my statement concerning the way Lunars affect Creation. I see them as Weird Gardner's in Creation, creating fragile, beautiful* marvels that don't hold up well when exposed to Creation's more banal aspects. They're caretakers for the Forest of Child-like Tree's, Vampire Lords for the cannibal cult that live in the dark heart of the city beneath Nexus, the secret shepherds to the People of Glass whose stories burn upon their bodies.<br /> <br /> The Solar have returned to tell you they carry miracles back to the world. The Sidereal's will tell you that (okay, they won't, but they will intuit it to you while you don't know about them) miracles are dead. The Lunar will take you down the secret paths, showing you that magic was hiding under your nose the whole time.<br /> <br /> *In case it isn't obvious, beautiful and terrible or beautiful and atrocious are interchangeable here. The Gardens of Raksi and Ma-Ha-Suchi are as horrifying as you imagine, and graceful enough to break your heart.<br /> <br /> Screw Alex Mercer, the ideal Lunar is Coyote.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron-crowns.obsidianportal.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron...dianportal.com</a> Visit Golden Shackles, Iron Crowns; a 3rd Edition Exalted Campaign ongoing since 2014","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2711-janissary87","name":"Janissary87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2711_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-04T22:16:56-07:00","id":125562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/124434-should-lunars-be-able-to-magically-affect-the-world-around-them?p=124941#post124941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Elaborate, please!</div> </div> </div> </div>Essentially, make it its own whole subsystem. Sort of like playing SimCity but with magical structures with X effect and three tiers of escalating awesome.<br /> <br /> I pointed what I wanted to call those earlier.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1252-god_of_awesome","name":"God_of_Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1252_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-05T01:04:00-07:00","id":125629,"title":"","content":"Lunars are losing their Wyld-specific (Wyld Keyword) Charms in EX3, and will go about as far backwards as you can get in terms of turning the world wibbly-wobbly. They shape themselves and they shape perceptions of themselves. (This statement does not reflect Evocations, Martial Arts or Sorcery.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/86-john-m\u00f8rke","name":"John M\u00f8rke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar86_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-05T01:39:55-07:00","id":125641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/124434-should-lunars-be-able-to-magically-affect-the-world-around-them?p=125629#post125629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lunars are losing their Wyld-specific (Wyld Keyword) Charms in EX3, and will go about as far backwards as you can get in terms of turning the world wibbly-wobbly. They shape themselves and they shape perceptions of themselves. (This statement does not reflect Evocations, Martial Arts or Sorcery.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I see, then this just means that the world shaping powers if we wanted them to be Lunar centric, means that Lunar sorcerers developed them as spells. I still really like the idea of the worldshaping secrets gleaned from Gaia by Luna, and shared through visions/dreams to her Chosen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-05T09:32:54-07:00","id":125876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/124434-should-lunars-be-able-to-magically-affect-the-world-around-them?p=125629#post125629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lunars are losing their Wyld-specific (Wyld Keyword) Charms in EX3, and will go about as far backwards as you can get in terms of turning the world wibbly-wobbly. They shape themselves and they shape perceptions of themselves. (This statement does not reflect Evocations, Martial Arts or Sorcery.)</div> </div> </div> </div>This is promising news! I don't really mind territory powers <i>per se</i>, but Lunars have never had a strong thesis informing their powers, and it sounds like 3e is being written with strong ideas about how to change that.<br /> <br /> I was not a big fan of Lunars having a lot of Wyld-focused powers, because while it makes sense that they'd be the Exalted with the most faciltiy at working with the Wyld (as opposed to imposing non-Wyld-ness on it, as WST does), it also presented them as &quot;belonging&quot; in the Wyld, which helped to justify their absence from and irrelevance to Creation proper. I wouldn't mind seeing the odd thing like an Intelligence charm that allows you to find cheaty routes through the Wyld, or something like that, but the way 2e handled it had some of the same thematic/focus issues as Spectral.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-05T09:46:29-07:00","id":125891,"title":"","content":"I would still be interested in the idea that there's a priority in the Silver Pact to try and code reality reinforcing and Fair Folk warding magic into the kinds of societies that are most likely to spring up in their wake, just for the sake of them having an eye towards a future in which the Realm and its satellites have been crushed (as well as certain contemporary practicalities where they dislike having to compete for control over peripheral societies with the raksha).<br /> <br /> This isn't a thing to encompass in Charms, or even Sorcery; rather a matter of complex long-term projects to spin stories out of.<br /> <br /> It may prove useful to people other than the Lunars in the course of seeing Creation through the Time of Tumult.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-05T12:47:37-07:00","id":126063,"title":"","content":"I echo the sentiment that there doesnt need to be a new system for lunars as they have access to celestial grade sorcery and necromancy. i will also agree that they need serious charm expansion beyond what is detailed in their splatbook. they have recieved the least amount of expansion with the exception of the sidereals (not counting the faefolk, alchemicals etc)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/779-nusoardgraphite","name":"NuSoardGraphite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar779_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-05T16:11:32-07:00","id":126216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/124434-should-lunars-be-able-to-magically-affect-the-world-around-them?p=125629#post125629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lunars are losing their Wyld-specific (Wyld Keyword) Charms in EX3, and will go about as far backwards as you can get in terms of turning the world wibbly-wobbly.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, Ritual of Lunar Stability is probably returning... but Harmony With Reality Technique might be very different, since dragging pieces of chaos into Creation is introducing wibbly-wobbly elements into an ordered system.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They shape themselves and they shape perceptions of themselves. </div> </div> </div>Interesting.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}